# NEVER commit generated wallets: these files contain private keys.
wallets*.json
*.wallets.json
keys*.json
password.txt

# Bare key files passed to --key-file (e.g. a seeder key kept outside the
# wallet exports). One line, 64 hex chars, and nothing else in the file.
*.key
key-*.txt

# BIP39 phrase files for gen_wallets.py --mnemonic-file. A phrase is strictly
# more powerful than any single private key: it regenerates all of them.
mnemonic.txt
phrase.txt
*.phrase
*.seed

# Scan output lists every address you own in one file -- public data, but it
# ties the whole set together, so keep it out of version control.
_scan*.json
scan-results.json

# Watch-only exports embed the account zpub: no funds at risk, but the key
# reveals every address and balance, so keep it out of version control too.
watch-only*.txt

# Payment request sheets (payment_request.py): public addresses and amounts, no
# secrets -- but every address of yours in one file, tied together. Send it to
# the payer; don't publish it in history.
payment-request*.csv
payment-request*.md

# Source private key for distribute_eth.py. NEVER commit this.
# Better still: keep it outside the project entirely.
source.key
*.key
*.privkey
key.txt

# Compiled token artifacts and the OpenZeppelin sources downloaded into them.
# No secrets -- both are regenerated by build_token.py -- but they are large and
# pinned to an exact compiler/version pair, so they do not belong in history.
build/

# Deployment and mint records hold the contract address together with the owner
# and operator addresses, i.e. a link between this token and the wallet files
# above. The chain itself is the authoritative record, so keep these local.
deployment-*.json
mint-*.json

# Token distribution records list every recipient address next to the token and
# the sending wallet, i.e. a map of the whole set. Keep them local too.
distribution-token-*.json

# Etherscan API key for verify_token.py (one key covers every chain, including
# Polygon). *.key above already covers etherscan.key; these are the other habits.
*.apikey
api-key.txt

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# CI writes the per-interpreter freeze here to upload it as an artifact.
resolved-py*.txt

# Address maps produced by the tools above. Public data, no keys -- but each one
# ties the whole set of your addresses together, which is the same reason the
# distribution and payment-request records above stay local. force-add one
# (`git add -f <file>`) if you decide a particular snapshot should be public.
distribution*.json
next100.txt
fund-targets*.txt
holders-*.csv
seed-transfer.json
seed-signer.txt
